# onnxruntime-node (pulled in by @huggingface/transformers) downloads ~270 MB of CUDA libraries from
# api.nuget.org in its postinstall on Linux x64 (Hostinger's build machines). The AI runs in the browser
# (onnxruntime-web), so the server never uses them: skip the download. The CPU binding ships in the npm
# package itself. npm hands this key to install scripts as npm_config_onnxruntime_node_install=skip:
# npm 10 (bundled with Node 22) silently, npm 11 with one "Unknown project config" warning. npm says a
# later major version will stop passing unknown keys; if a build log shows the nuget.org download
# again, set the environment variable ONNXRUNTIME_NODE_INSTALL=skip for the build instead.
onnxruntime-node-install=skip
